WEBVTT

01:03:59.775 --> 01:04:01.488
they're not at stake.

01:04:01.512 --> 01:04:03.348
They're not thinking about themselves.

01:04:03.372 --> 01:04:05.761
They're living a life
that genuinely is for others.

01:04:05.785 --> 01:04:09.285
And I used to think that was impossible,
that everybody's sort of selfish,

01:04:09.309 --> 01:04:10.464
which is sort of true.

01:04:10.488 --> 01:04:12.111
But I've seen it so many times --

01:04:12.135 --> 01:04:16.190
these weavers, they literally live
for others, and they radiate joy.

01:04:16.214 --> 01:04:17.960
CA: Speaking of evolutionary quirks,

01:04:17.984 --> 01:04:22.735
it is weird that people who live
for others seem to get joy from it.

01:04:22.759 --> 01:04:25.248
It's not clear to me
why evolution would allow that.

01:04:25.272 --> 01:04:27.021
DB: Yeah, the theory would be,

01:04:27.045 --> 01:04:29.987
we didn't survive because
we were really strong or fast.